WEBVTT

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.330
Hey! You there! Halt!

00:00:18.410 --> 00:00:20.040
Not again.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:22.080
You're Deflotte Danois, aren't you?

00:00:21.910 --> 00:00:26.790
"Former bounty hunter"
"Deflotte Danois"

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:27.740
You are suspected of larceny, molestation,
and arson in Tours!

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:29.580
I'm telling you,

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:32.410
those accusations are false!

00:00:32.410 --> 00:00:34.580
--What is that?!
--A smoke bomb!

00:00:34.580 --> 00:00:35.660
Bye, now.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:37.050
Damn it!

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:38.660
Where did he go?!

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.080
Don't let him escape! Come on!

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:41.080
Right!

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:45.910
For the love of...
Open your eyes, why don't you?

00:00:45.910 --> 00:00:49.870
Huh?! They only want five gold coins for me?!

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:53.120
The mug shot, though... is not half bad.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:27.620
In order to advise the young King Charlot,

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:31.910
newly ascended to the throne
following Duke Rugis's uprising,

00:02:31.910 --> 00:02:35.040
Pope Vall d'Hebron, of the Orthodox Church,

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:38.410
has taken up the position of guardian.

00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:43.200
In effect, the Hortensian Orthodox Church
has assumed control of the land,

00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:46.580
and the royal order of knights
has been placed under the supervision

00:02:46.580 --> 00:02:48.450
of the Ecclesiastical Order.

00:02:54.740 --> 00:02:56.950
How is it, being in the capital after all this time?

00:02:56.950 --> 00:02:58.240
Yeah...

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:01.330
It looks like things have pretty well recovered now.

00:03:03.080 --> 00:03:03.950
What is it?

00:03:03.950 --> 00:03:08.490
Oh, I'm just concerned about Marius.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.580
You're going to the capital?!

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:12.950
There's obviously something up with this!

00:03:12.950 --> 00:03:15.290
Where's this suddenly coming from, Marius?

00:03:15.290 --> 00:03:18.700
This is a summons from the captain
of the Ecclesiastical Order himself.

00:03:18.700 --> 00:03:21.450
The Ecclesiastical Order <i>is</i> the issue!

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:24.870
What if they start some kind of trouble,
and you get thrown in prison?

00:03:24.870 --> 00:03:28.700
They aren't going to arrest Alfred
because he hasn't done anything.

00:03:28.700 --> 00:03:30.290
Even so...

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:35.120
Marius, I was a royal knight
before I became the lord here.

00:03:35.120 --> 00:03:36.910
I know.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:40.450
But even so, I don't...

00:03:40.450 --> 00:03:41.790
Marius...

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.120
I'm sure he has his reasons.

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:50.450
Just be understanding when the time comes.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:51.450
Yeah.

00:03:56.040 --> 00:03:57.080
I have to ask,

00:03:57.080 --> 00:04:02.950
what is Georg up to, sending us a call-up
notice with nothing written on it?

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.410
You're acquaintances with Captain Georg, aren't you?

00:04:05.410 --> 00:04:09.120
Sort of, way back during my time in the royal order.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:11.200
The man is someone who can be trusted.

00:04:14.120 --> 00:04:15.580
It looks like I've been keeping you.

00:04:18.190 --> 00:04:22.740
"Hortensian Orthodox Church Ecclesiastical Order Captain"
"Georg Dalmas"

00:04:18.740 --> 00:04:23.040
And after I asked you to come to me, too. Forgive me.

00:04:23.040 --> 00:04:26.700
Not at all. You invited us personally, after all.

00:04:26.700 --> 00:04:30.330
Captain Georg, it is an honor to see you again.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.950
That's right. I haven't seen you since
your investiture ceremony, have I?

00:04:33.950 --> 00:04:35.870
Who would have thought that the day would come

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.290
when I would stand shoulder-to-shoulder
with Fernando's son?

00:04:38.290 --> 00:04:40.790
I think that's enough with the pleasantries.

00:04:40.790 --> 00:04:44.990
Come on, you called us up here for this.

00:04:44.990 --> 00:04:48.910
Is it something you don't want others to hear about?

00:04:48.910 --> 00:04:51.200
I see you're as perceptive as ever.

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:57.990
Do you remember the petridermic plague
that erupted in Petale Village two years ago?

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.620
Sure. It was a strange disease
that made the skin hard and gray,

00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:02.910
virtually turning people into stone statues.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:05.330
They gathered physicians from around the kingdom,

00:05:05.330 --> 00:05:07.490
but they couldn't find any way to treat it,

00:05:07.490 --> 00:05:11.620
and the Orthodox Church had no choice
but to quarantine the whole village.

00:05:11.620 --> 00:05:13.200
I hear that it is a ghost town now,

00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:16.330
and no one is permitted to go in or out of the village.

00:05:16.330 --> 00:05:20.240
I want you two to conduct an off-the-books
investigation into Petale Village.

00:05:20.240 --> 00:05:21.240
Huh?

00:05:21.240 --> 00:05:23.910
As it happens, there have been a number of sightings

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:28.290
of monsters that look like people
in the vicinity of the village recently.

00:05:28.290 --> 00:05:30.910
In the words of those who saw them...

00:05:30.910 --> 00:05:34.700
"It looked as though there were
dead bodies walking around."

00:05:34.700 --> 00:05:36.540
Walking corpses?

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:39.830
Sounds just like the undead of Magonian lore.

00:05:39.830 --> 00:05:42.490
I don't know if this is connected
with the petridermic plague,

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:44.870
but we must avoid having the name of Petale Village

00:05:44.870 --> 00:05:47.830
striking new terror into the hearts of the people.

00:05:47.830 --> 00:05:48.790
But Captain,

00:05:48.790 --> 00:05:53.040
shouldn't you dispatch your own men to deal with this?

00:05:55.370 --> 00:05:56.490
All right!

00:05:56.490 --> 00:06:00.370
We'll do as you ask! Right, Alfred?

00:06:01.450 --> 00:06:06.120
Very well. We will go and discreetly look around.

00:06:06.120 --> 00:06:07.370
Thanks.

00:06:09.040 --> 00:06:11.740
I don't care if you <i>did</i> know him
a long time ago, Maurice,

00:06:11.740 --> 00:06:14.040
an investigation involving the church is just...

00:06:14.040 --> 00:06:18.450
Captain Georg doesn't want the tragedy
of Petale Village to be repeated.

00:06:18.450 --> 00:06:21.660
The Orthodox Church sacrificed this village.

00:06:21.660 --> 00:06:24.950
I'm sure you aren't ignorant of
the stories about a witch, are you?

00:06:24.950 --> 00:06:27.580
What stories about a witch <i>moru</i> ?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:30.370
It's said that the petridermic plague was a curse,

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:33.410
invoked by a witch trying to destroy the kingdom.

00:06:33.410 --> 00:06:36.080
"Quarantine the village, and seal it off.

00:06:36.080 --> 00:06:40.740
Otherwise, the witch's curse
will swallow up all of Hortensia."

00:06:40.740 --> 00:06:43.200
As the people of the kingdom grew scared of the stories,

00:06:43.200 --> 00:06:47.330
the Orthodox Church pledged to put
the petridermic plague witch to death,

00:06:47.330 --> 00:06:50.910
and placed an all-but-permanent
lockdown on Petale Village.

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.910
The Orthodox Church is still looking
for the witch even now.

00:06:56.620 --> 00:06:59.540
But does this witch really even exist?

00:06:59.540 --> 00:07:02.410
The church is just preying on the people's fear

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:07.160
and using it to steer the kingdom
the way they want, aren't they?!

00:07:07.160 --> 00:07:08.370
Marius...

00:07:08.370 --> 00:07:10.660
Oh... Sorry.

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:15.080
I get that you don't have a very high
opinion of the Orthodox Church.

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:20.160
But when you talk like that,
it makes you more liable to get arrested.

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:22.950
I know. I'll be careful.

00:07:25.040 --> 00:07:26.240
<i>Moru</i> ...

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:34.240
Indeed, quite the ambience here.

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:36.120
The fence was broken through.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:38.120
Someone must have entered here.

00:07:38.120 --> 00:07:40.450
It could be the work of the "undead," too.

00:07:42.950 --> 00:07:45.080
I wonder if this really works...

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:46.040
That flower...

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.580
Oh, this is, um...

00:07:47.580 --> 00:07:48.950
That sure takes me back.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:49.950
Huh?

00:07:49.950 --> 00:07:54.700
Nonnoria listened to Ber's stories long ago,
and picked some of those.

00:07:54.700 --> 00:07:56.450
Oh, she did?

00:07:56.450 --> 00:08:02.370
As long as you have this flower,
the undead will be driven away in no time!

00:08:02.370 --> 00:08:03.950
I-In no time?

00:08:03.950 --> 00:08:05.450
What flower is it <i>moru</i> ?

00:08:05.450 --> 00:08:11.870
This is a Requiem flower. You just hold up
this flower, and say the incantation.

00:08:11.870 --> 00:08:17.120
" <i>Hinfort, hinfort, bevor das</i> ..."

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.120
Oh, just a minute! " <i>Hinfort</i> "?

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.870
Yes, it's a passage meant to soothe
the souls of the dead spirits,

00:08:19.870 --> 00:08:21.370
according to Magonian lore.

00:08:21.370 --> 00:08:23.540
It's not as though I believe in that!

00:08:23.540 --> 00:08:25.290
And it's not like I'm afraid of undead, either--

00:08:25.290 --> 00:08:27.990
Wah! Stop! Stay back!

00:08:27.990 --> 00:08:29.410
There's someone here!

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:39.580
What is going on here?

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:50.700
Damn it!

00:08:53.660 --> 00:08:55.040
Over there <i>moru</i> !

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.620
Ho...

00:08:59.620 --> 00:09:00.660
Damn...

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.330
Are those undead?

00:09:02.330 --> 00:09:05.120
Marius, do the incantation <i>moru</i> !

00:09:05.120 --> 00:09:07.580
A-All right.

00:09:07.580 --> 00:09:10.410
<i>Hinfort, hinfort</i> ,

00:09:10.410 --> 00:09:13.660
<i>bevor das Lied endet</i> ...

00:09:13.660 --> 00:09:14.790
What the...?

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:19.490
<i>Bevor der Duft der Blume vergeht</i> ...!

00:09:19.490 --> 00:09:20.490
It worked!

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:22.450
They stopped moving <i>moru</i> !

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.120
It didn't work at all <i>moru</i> !

00:09:25.120 --> 00:09:27.120
Why are they coming this way?!

00:09:33.660 --> 00:09:35.410
Hey, you!

00:09:40.700 --> 00:09:41.910
Ho...

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:47.330
Look at Alfred.

00:09:47.330 --> 00:09:49.620
He took care of them almost all by himself.

00:09:59.870 --> 00:10:01.620
What happened here?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:03.790
That's what I'd like to know.

00:10:03.790 --> 00:10:05.910
What are all of you doing here, anyway?

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:08.290
We're here because the Orthodox Ch--

00:10:08.290 --> 00:10:10.160
The Orthodox Church?!

00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:13.490
Take it easy.

00:10:13.490 --> 00:10:19.080
I'm a pleasant enough old man
who enjoys looking after his dear nephew!

00:10:19.080 --> 00:10:21.120
One who was formerly a royal knight.

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:24.700
A royal knight? Then you <i>are</i> one
of the Orthodox Church's dogs!

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:28.620
Circumstances brought us here
to put down the village's undead.

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:30.410
I'm Alfred.

00:10:30.410 --> 00:10:33.490
Why is it that you violated
the Orthodox Church's prohibition

00:10:33.490 --> 00:10:35.200
and came to this village?

00:10:35.200 --> 00:10:37.330
None of your business.

00:10:37.330 --> 00:10:40.910
And you there!
What was that you were just doing?!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:42.490
There's an old tradition

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:45.660
that says you can ward off undead
using a Requiem flower.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.660
Hmph.

00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:51.700
I don't know what brings you all
the way out here to kill monsters...

00:10:54.040 --> 00:10:55.910
but keep out of my way.

00:10:57.790 --> 00:10:59.370
H-Hey...

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.540
What's the deal with him?

00:11:13.950 --> 00:11:18.240
Without any people around,
things fall apart quite a bit, huh?

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:20.580
They called it the petridermic <i>plague</i> .

00:11:20.580 --> 00:11:22.950
It's little wonder that when
people can't move anymore,

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:24.910
they'd get pretty weather-beaten.

00:11:24.910 --> 00:11:27.870
They wouldn't get neglected, though.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:32.620
They'd either be gathered into a nursing home
or buried in the cemetery.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:37.410
No, even if they got buried in turn,
that would still leave one last person.

00:11:37.410 --> 00:11:41.330
It's strange that we haven't seen a single body.

00:11:41.330 --> 00:11:42.540
You don't suppose...!

00:11:44.120 --> 00:11:46.990
Why don't we go check out the cemetery?

00:11:47.950 --> 00:11:50.160
By the church. Let's go see.

00:11:51.580 --> 00:11:54.240
Marius, what's wrong maru?

00:11:54.240 --> 00:11:58.160
What I was saying earlier--
could it be...

00:11:58.160 --> 00:12:02.240
...that the villagers have turned
into undead, by any chance?

00:12:02.240 --> 00:12:05.160
Oh, is <i>that</i> what you were worried about?

00:12:05.160 --> 00:12:06.240
Still...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.540
Maurice, the monsters here were-- Oh, right...

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.290
What?

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:14.580
That's why he was acting like that.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:20.910
That man earlier is probably from this village.

00:12:20.910 --> 00:12:23.370
Huh? How can that be?

00:12:27.040 --> 00:12:30.740
I didn't realize Petale Village had such a fine church.

00:12:33.740 --> 00:12:37.660
They had a priest, too,
and they held regular worship services.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:40.740
How is there someone from
the locked-down Petale Village still here?

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:44.450
Because I fled the village a long time ago.

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.410
I had heard stories about the village
during my travels, though.

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:54.490
While this village may have been
forsaken by the rest of the kingdom,

00:12:54.490 --> 00:12:58.370
I thought that the least I could do
was come by and leave some flowers.

00:12:58.370 --> 00:13:01.740
You came back to mourn the other villagers?

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:07.120
But there's no sign of them ever being buried.
What exactly happened here?

00:13:07.120 --> 00:13:11.870
You didn't happen to see any familiar faces
among the undead, did you?

00:13:11.870 --> 00:13:14.120
Don't be ridiculous! Of course not!

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.490
No, I would think not.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.950
Huh? What does that mean?

00:13:19.950 --> 00:13:25.290
Four years ago, I happened to be
someplace where monsters appeared.

00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:30.040
They come here from some other
plane through magic circles.

00:13:30.040 --> 00:13:32.870
Never once have I ever heard of people or creatures

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:37.410
who were originally from this world
turning into monsters.

00:13:37.410 --> 00:13:40.370
Which means that those undead
were not citizens of Petale Village

00:13:40.370 --> 00:13:43.950
whose bitter resentment had turned them into monsters.

00:13:43.950 --> 00:13:45.410
Rest easy, lad.

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:52.120
So that's why you were acting so funny before.

00:13:52.120 --> 00:13:53.830
What's your name?

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.290
Oh, my name's Deflotte.

00:13:57.290 --> 00:14:00.080
Something inside the church might tell us something.

00:14:00.080 --> 00:14:01.870
Would you mind showing us around?

00:14:01.870 --> 00:14:06.450
Once that's done, let us help you mourn the villagers.

00:14:06.450 --> 00:14:07.740
Would that be all right?

00:14:10.160 --> 00:14:11.990
Suit yourselves.

00:14:20.540 --> 00:14:22.910
I don't think you're going to find much of anything.

00:14:26.950 --> 00:14:28.290
What's this?

00:14:30.990 --> 00:14:33.540
This must be the priest's journal.

00:14:33.540 --> 00:14:34.700
Let's have a look.

00:14:34.700 --> 00:14:36.200
Here, let me see that!

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:43.910
"September 20. The word of
the pope has reached our village.

00:14:43.910 --> 00:14:47.120
It says that the sickness that turns people to stone...

00:14:47.120 --> 00:14:51.160
is a trial bestowed upon our land by God.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:56.330
We have also been forbidden to leave the village."

00:14:56.330 --> 00:15:03.490
"November 2. Those who cannot endure
this trial are neither granted salvation.

00:15:03.490 --> 00:15:08.870
Will God forgive me when I am so powerless?"

00:15:08.870 --> 00:15:15.450
"November 18. All we can do
is stay here and pray to God.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:18.370
And so we pray, asking over and over,

00:15:18.370 --> 00:15:25.790
'O God, why must we bear the entirety
of this world's despair?'"

00:15:27.830 --> 00:15:31.950
Why... Why did you rely on God right to the end...

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:35.370
...Pop?!

00:15:36.700 --> 00:15:40.330
You're the son of the church's priest?

00:15:40.330 --> 00:15:43.580
Yeah. And I hated it, so I left the village.

00:15:45.200 --> 00:15:49.410
Ever since I was little, I was more
proud of my pop than anything,

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:51.790
for the way that all the other villagers respected him.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:56.410
But when my ma passed,
he insisted that I become a priest,

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.620
and we fought about it every day.

00:15:58.620 --> 00:16:03.290
When I left, he drove me away
and as much as disowned me.

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:06.330
But when my pop and the others
were suffering like this,

00:16:06.330 --> 00:16:09.330
what did I think I was doing?

00:16:10.540 --> 00:16:11.620
Deflotte...

00:16:12.950 --> 00:16:14.990
That's enough!

00:16:14.990 --> 00:16:16.540
Don't anyone move!

00:16:16.540 --> 00:16:18.790
Ecclesiastical knights! When did <i>they</i> get here?!

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:21.580
This is going to be a problem.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.870
You must be the ones who are
trespassing on forbidden ground,

00:16:23.870 --> 00:16:28.700
and are now trying to bring those
with the petridermic plague back to life!

00:16:28.700 --> 00:16:32.620
We cannot permit you to set loose
the witch's curse from this land.

00:16:32.620 --> 00:16:36.580
Set fire to them! We'll burn them along
with the village to purge the curse!

00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:37.740
Burn the village?!

00:16:37.740 --> 00:16:38.830
That's absurd!

00:16:40.040 --> 00:16:42.240
Screw you all!

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:45.290
Was forsaking the village alone not good enough?!

00:16:45.290 --> 00:16:50.290
The villagers of Petale were sacrificed
to allay the witch's curse.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:55.990
The people of this village died seeking
answers from the God you serve!

00:16:55.990 --> 00:16:59.120
You're telling me that answer is
"burn it down"?!

00:16:59.120 --> 00:17:02.740
What kind of filthy son of a bitch is your God?!

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:04.620
Enough.

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:06.790
We will dispose of you right here and now!

00:17:11.240 --> 00:17:14.080
You mere royal knight...!

00:17:14.080 --> 00:17:18.540
Do you realize what it means to defy
the Ecclesiastical Knights?

00:17:18.540 --> 00:17:23.290
He's only here to mourn his family
and friends in the village!

00:17:23.290 --> 00:17:25.540
I don't care if you're the
Orthodox Church or a knight.

00:17:25.540 --> 00:17:28.120
You can't stop him from doing that!

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:29.490
Are you...?

00:17:29.490 --> 00:17:30.910
How dare you.

00:17:32.330 --> 00:17:34.790
Wh-What is that?!

00:17:34.790 --> 00:17:36.540
Did you summon him?!

00:17:45.540 --> 00:17:47.290
There's even one of these here?

00:17:47.290 --> 00:17:48.490
He's huge.

00:17:58.040 --> 00:18:00.620
What regenerative abilities it has!

00:18:02.700 --> 00:18:04.910
Marius, look <i>moru</i> !

00:18:04.910 --> 00:18:06.160
Are those...?

00:18:06.160 --> 00:18:09.200
So many Requiem flowers <i>moru</i> !

00:18:09.200 --> 00:18:10.740
With this many of them, we can take him!

00:18:10.740 --> 00:18:11.950
You idiots!

00:18:11.950 --> 00:18:14.580
The majority of the flowers
here are Immortelles.

00:18:14.580 --> 00:18:19.240
Legend has it that the dead who rose
ate those to try to sustain themselves!

00:18:19.240 --> 00:18:23.660
Are you saying that it's because
of these flowers that he's so huge?

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:25.330
You bastard!

00:18:27.700 --> 00:18:29.040
Damn!

00:18:29.040 --> 00:18:30.330
Deflotte!

00:18:34.240 --> 00:18:37.290
As I remember the legend,
what returned the dead back into the ground

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:41.370
was a single Requiem flower
blooming among the Immortelles!

00:18:41.370 --> 00:18:42.990
Then, it must be somewhere!

00:18:42.990 --> 00:18:44.910
But where <i>moru</i> ?

00:18:45.910 --> 00:18:47.740
Right here! Hurry!

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:49.580
Oh, right!

00:18:50.910 --> 00:18:52.120
I'm using it!

00:18:52.120 --> 00:18:56.990
<i>Hinfort, hinfort, bevor das Lied endet.</i>

00:18:56.990 --> 00:19:00.990
<i>Bevor der Duft der Blume vergeht,</i>

00:19:00.990 --> 00:19:04.370
<i>bevor der Wunsch vergessen ist.</i>

00:19:04.370 --> 00:19:08.040
<i>Hinfort mit euch an jenen Ort</i> !

00:19:34.160 --> 00:19:37.490
Thank for this, Deflotte.

00:19:37.490 --> 00:19:38.490
Sure.

00:19:39.830 --> 00:19:42.120
Ma always did like these flowers.

00:19:50.790 --> 00:19:56.620
"I am, at the last, the only person
remaining in Petale Village.

00:19:56.620 --> 00:20:03.040
O God, I wish to express my gratitude
that Deflotte is not here.

00:20:03.040 --> 00:20:06.540
As long as that boy is still safe,

00:20:06.540 --> 00:20:11.330
I will gladly accept this trial."

00:20:13.410 --> 00:20:17.620
Thinking about me, right up
to the very end? Honestly...

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:22.240
Rest in peace, Pop.

00:20:27.450 --> 00:20:31.660
That Ecclesiastical Knight knew
that you were a royal knight.

00:20:31.660 --> 00:20:35.200
Unless Captain Georg revealed
that information, that's not possible.

00:20:35.200 --> 00:20:39.330
We can't be certain that it was
the captain who sent them here.

00:20:39.330 --> 00:20:42.490
We'll go to the capital to deliver our report.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:44.990
We'll ask the captain what his
real motives are when we do.

00:20:48.700 --> 00:20:49.950
What's this?

00:20:49.950 --> 00:20:52.080
Are you all still here?

00:20:52.080 --> 00:20:56.830
What the hell are you talking about?
We're waiting for you, of course.

00:20:56.830 --> 00:20:58.620
Huh? What for?

00:20:58.620 --> 00:21:03.330
You have nowhere to go, do you?
Do you feel like tagging along with us?

00:21:03.330 --> 00:21:04.910
Why me?

00:21:04.910 --> 00:21:07.740
Because you have what it takes to be a knight.

00:21:07.740 --> 00:21:08.870
A knight?!

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:13.160
I'd need the recommendation
of someone important for that!

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:19.580
Let me start over. I'm Alfred Albert,
lord of the Albert Dominion.

00:21:19.580 --> 00:21:22.490
I think you're more than worthy
of my recommendation.

00:21:22.490 --> 00:21:24.490
Are you serious?

00:21:24.490 --> 00:21:28.490
I've seen your devotion to your homeland.

00:21:28.490 --> 00:21:33.660
As a lord, I need men like you
to keep my people safe.

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:36.330
Come with me, Deflotte.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:43.620
Well, that might not be so bad, either.

00:21:45.740 --> 00:21:49.240
Very well. I'll accompany you to Albert.

00:21:49.240 --> 00:21:51.830
Yeah. I'm looking forward to it.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.040
Chapter 3

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.040
Repose                      of Souls

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.040
~To the Quarantined Village~

00:23:33.540 --> 00:23:35.290
What shall we do, Your Majesty?

00:23:35.290 --> 00:23:36.240
Did you say slave?

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:37.790
There's nothing to worry about now.

00:23:37.790 --> 00:23:38.990
I never said that.

00:23:38.990 --> 00:23:40.950
Right now, it's my turn to be right.

00:23:40.950 --> 00:23:43.040
I can't stand to just sit around and wait.

00:23:43.040 --> 00:23:47.040
We are knights. We cannot back down!

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:47.030
Chapter 4

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:47.030
Turnabout

00:23:44.040 --> 00:23:47.030
~Prelude to Turmoil~
